
# NDT Certificate Automation System

A web-based certificate automation platform designed to streamline the creation and management of inspection certificates for Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) and inspection companies.

This system was built to solve a real operational documentation problem encountered while working as an NDT Inspection Technician.

---

## Features

- Automated high-quality PDF certificate generation using Puppeteer
- Reusable browser-based certificate templates
- Support for company branding elements:
  - Letterheads
  - Stamps
  - Signatures
  - Equipment images
- Full CRUD functionality for certificate templates
- Clean NestJS modular architecture
- MongoDB for data persistence
- Server-rendered interfaces using EJS
- Designed for easy expansion into other certificate-based industries

---

## Tech Stack

| Category          | Technology              |
|-------------------|-------------------------|
| Framework         | NestJS                  |
| Language          | TypeScript              |
| Database          | MongoDB + Mongoose      |
| PDF Generation    | Puppeteer               |
| Templating        | EJS                     |
| Validation        | class-validator         |
| Architecture      | Modular NestJS design   |

---

## Project Structure (Typical)

src/
├── certificates/           # Certificate module
├── templates/              # Template management
├── pdf/                    # PDF generation logic (Puppeteer)
├── auth/                   # Authentication (if implemented)
├── views/                  # EJS templates
├── utils/
└── main.ts

---

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js v18 or higher
- MongoDB (local or Atlas)
- Git

### Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/TechieJoe/YOUR-NDT-REPO-NAME.git

# Navigate into the project
cd YOUR-NDT-REPO-NAME

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Environment Variables
Create a .env file in the root directory:
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/ndt-certificates
PORT=3000

# Running the Application

# Development mode
npm run start:dev

# Production mode
npm run build

The application will be available at:
http://localhost:3000

# Key Highlights

Built from a real industry pain point (manual certificate preparation)
Significantly reduces the time required to generate professional certificates
Supports company-specific branding
Structured for future scalability and multi-industry use

